How to fix:
Make the value operand of `CALL` authoritative: before dispatching the nested call, verify the caller holds sufficient spendable balance for the requested value and perform the actual debit/credit through the host layer (the same `transfer_attos_in_unit` path used by `universal_call`), reverting on insufficient balance. Until that transfer is wired in, refuse any non-zero CALL value explicitly instead of silently ignoring it, so a callee can never observe a `CALLVALUE` that was never paid. Add a regression test that a value-bearing CALL with insufficient balance reverts and that a funded CALL moves exactly the requested amount.

Please fix this vulnerability. If you propose a fix, make it concise and minimal.
