### 🔴 Seat-quorum finality lets a minimum-stake validator coalition finalize alone

**Severity:** HIGH · **CWE-863**

The new finality committee caps any validator at a quarter of the seats and then hands every seat the cap leaves over to the smallest validators, so seat weight stops tracking stake. With one validator holding almost all the stake and a handful of validators at the registry's minimum stake, the small validators receive 96 of 128 seats while the quorum is 86. The PR also deletes the stake quorum from the BLS finality path, so nothing else weighs their stake. A coalition of minimum-stake validators can therefore finalize checkpoints alone and the dominant stake holder cannot stop it, while light clients, which still require the stake quorum, reject the certificates the nodes accept.

```suggestion
    fn check_prevote_quorum(&mut self) {
        // Quorum is counted in seats (section 7.4.3): a voter signs once and
        // covers every seat it holds. The seat quorum alone is not a safety
        // bound: the table caps a validator at a quarter of the seats and hands
        // the surplus to the smallest validators, so a coalition holding almost
        // no stake can cover it. The stake quorum stays alongside it.
        let covered = self.committee.covered_seats(self.prevotes.keys());
        let voted_stake: u128 = self
            .prevotes
            .keys()
            .filter_map(|addr| self.validator_snapshot.find_validator(addr))
            .map(|validator| u128::from(validator.stake))
            .sum();
        if covered >= self.committee.quorum_seats()
            && voted_stake >= self.validator_snapshot.quorum_stake()
        {
            self.prevote_quorum_reached = true;
        }
    }

    fn check_precommit_quorum(&mut self) {
        let covered = self.committee.covered_seats(self.precommits.keys());
        let voted_stake: u128 = self
            .precommits
            .keys()
            .filter_map(|addr| self.validator_snapshot.find_validator(addr))
            .map(|validator| u128::from(validator.stake))
            .sum();
        if covered >= self.committee.quorum_seats()
            && voted_stake >= self.validator_snapshot.quorum_stake()
        {
            self.precommit_quorum_reached = true;
        }
    }
```

