### 🔴 Unmetered EVM memory expansion lets a single cheap transaction abort the node process

**Severity:** HIGH · **CWE-789**

The EVM interpreter added in this PR (`run_evm_bytecode` in `src/execution/coordinator/evm_ee.rs`) never charges memory-expansion gas and never caps interpreter memory. Every opcode is charged a flat 3 gas, while MSTORE, MLOAD, KECCAK256, CALLDATACOPY, LOG, CALL, CREATE2, RETURN and REVERT accept attacker-supplied 64-bit offsets and lengths (`U256Word::to_usize_checked` only rejects values wider than 64 bits) and then grow the interpreter buffer with `mem.resize(off + len, 0)` or allocate `vec![0u8; len]`. A deployed contract therefore reaches a multi-terabyte allocation for a few gas. Because the default coordinator registers `EvmEe` through `WorkerEndpoint::in_process`, without the address-space limit that only applies to Unix-socket workers, the allocation happens inside the node process; Rust aborts the process on allocation failure and `catch_unwind` cannot intercept it, so one transaction kills the node. This finding is from source review only: the PR head does not compile, so the crash was not reproduced dynamically.

```suggestion
/// Hard ceiling on interpreter memory, independent of gas.
pub const MAX_EVM_MEMORY_BYTES: usize = 16 * 1024 * 1024;

/// EVM memory-expansion cost for growing the highest touched word from `old` to `new`.
fn memory_expansion_gas(old_bytes: usize, new_bytes: usize) -> u64 {
    let words = |n: usize| (n as u64).div_ceil(32);
    let square = |w: u64| w.saturating_mul(w) / 512;
    let (old_w, new_w) = (words(old_bytes), words(new_bytes));
    3u64.saturating_mul(new_w.saturating_sub(old_w))
        .saturating_add(square(new_w).saturating_sub(square(old_w)))
}

/// Charges expansion gas and grows `mem` to cover `offset..offset + len`.
fn grow_mem(
    mem: &mut Vec<u8>,
    host: &mut dyn HostApi,
    offset: usize,
    len: usize,
) -> Result<(), String> {
    let Some(need) = offset.checked_add(len) else {
        return Err(String::from("evm memory overflow"));
    };
    if need > MAX_EVM_MEMORY_BYTES {
        return Err(String::from("evm memory limit exceeded"));
    }
    if need > mem.len() {
        host.charge(memory_expansion_gas(mem.len(), need))
            .map_err(|_| String::from("out of gas in memory expansion"))?;
        mem.resize(need, 0);
    }
    Ok(())
}

fn mem_read_32(mem: &mut Vec<u8>, offset: usize) -> [u8; 32] {
    let need = offset.saturating_add(32);
    if mem.len() < need {
        mem.resize(need, 0);
    }
    let mut out = [0u8; 32];
    if let Some(s) = mem.get(offset..offset + 32) {
        out.copy_from_slice(s);
    }
    out
}

fn mem_write(mem: &mut Vec<u8>, offset: usize, data: &[u8]) {
    if data.is_empty() {
        return;
    }
    let need = offset.saturating_add(data.len());
    if mem.len() < need {
        mem.resize(need, 0);
    }
    if let Some(dst) = mem.get_mut(offset..offset + data.len()) {
        dst.copy_from_slice(data);
    }
}
```

