### 🔵 Universal call transfers debit a worker-supplied source identity without authorization

**Severity:** MEDIUM · **CWE-639**

`HostBridge::universal_call` moves BUD for a value-bearing cross-environment call from whatever account the execution-environment worker places in `UniversalCall::from`. That field arrives unchanged from the worker over the host RPC path (`Op::UniversalCall` -&gt; `UniversalCall::try_from` -&gt; `host.universal_call`) and the coordinator neither ties it to the contract executing the current frame nor applies any authorization to the debit, in contrast to `bud_transfer` in the same file, which gates the identical transfer through `authorize_holding_access`. A compromised or faulty EE worker serving host callbacks can therefore debit any account into a destination it chooses, and the movement persists when the child frame is committed. The UEL coordinator has no block-execution caller yet, so this is not remotely triggerable on a running node today, but the check is missing from a fund-moving primitive in newly added core code.

