### 🔵 Compat Ethereum JSON-RPC handler builds a fresh gateway and hardcoded peer per request, so the peer quota never fires and every call deep-clones the full account state

**Severity:** MEDIUM · **CWE-770**

`handle_eth_jsonrpc` constructs a new `EthereumCompatGateway` on every call and passes the literal peer `127.0.0.1` with `now_secs = 0`, so the gateway's `PeerQuotaTracker` starts empty each time and `max_requests_per_window` never triggers; all callers also share one bucket instead of the connection identity the design requires. Each `eth_sendRawTransaction` then deep-clones the whole `AccountState` and re-runs envelope decode plus secp256k1 recovery before rejecting the input, and Cosmos `broadcast_tx_*` does the same with no limiter at all, so an unauthenticated client forces unbounded state-sized work per request. Accepted transactions are also appended to `staged_txs`, which has no capacity bound and no eviction. No listener serves these handlers in this tree yet; the weakness becomes remotely reachable once the documented compat listeners are wired.

```suggestion
pub fn handle_eth_jsonrpc(state: &AccountState, peer: &str, raw_json: &str) -> String {
    const QUOTA_WINDOW_SECS: u64 = 60;
    static ETH_GATEWAY: std::sync::Mutex<Option<EthereumCompatGateway>> =
        std::sync::Mutex::new(None);
    static QUOTA_WINDOW: std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64 =
        std::sync::atomic::AtomicU64::new(u64::MAX);

    if raw_json.len() > MAX_COMPAT_REQUEST_BYTES {
        let resp = JsonRpcResponse::err(
            serde_json::Value::Null,
            JSONRPC_LIMIT_EXCEEDED,
            "request payload exceeds MAX_COMPAT_REQUEST_BYTES",
        );
        return serde_json::to_string(&resp).unwrap_or_default();
    }
    let Ok(req) = serde_json::from_str::<JsonRpcRequest>(raw_json) else {
        let resp = JsonRpcResponse::err(serde_json::Value::Null, -32700, "Parse error");
        return serde_json::to_string(&resp).unwrap_or_default();
    };
    let now_secs = std::time::SystemTime::now()
        .duration_since(std::time::UNIX_EPOCH)
        .map_or(0, |d| d.as_secs());
    let window = now_secs / QUOTA_WINDOW_SECS;
    // One gateway serves every connection, so the per-peer quota and the staged
    // transaction table outlive a single request.
    let Ok(mut guard) = ETH_GATEWAY.lock() else {
        let resp = JsonRpcResponse::err(
            req.id.clone(),
            JSONRPC_LIMIT_EXCEEDED,
            "compatibility gateway unavailable",
        );
        return serde_json::to_string(&resp).unwrap_or_default();
    };
    let gw = guard
        .get_or_insert_with(|| EthereumCompatGateway::new(EthereumCompatConfig::default()));
    if QUOTA_WINDOW.swap(window, std::sync::atomic::Ordering::Relaxed) != window {
        gw.reset_quota_window();
    }
    let resp = gw.handle_request(CompatListener::Public, peer, now_secs, &req, state);
    drop(guard);
    serde_json::to_string(&resp).unwrap_or_default()
}
```

