### 🔴 SVM adapter mints any mint and overwrites any account without ownership or authority checks

**Severity:** HIGH · **CWE-862**

The in-process SVM environment registered by `ExecutionCoordinator::new()` turns an attacker-supplied `SvmInstructionEnvelope` straight into `ee/svm/account` writes with no ownership or authority check. `SplMintTo` never reads the mint and never compares the caller to the recorded mint authority, so any funded account can credit an arbitrary amount of any mint to an ATA derived from `dest_owner` and then move it on with `SplTransfer`. `SplInitializeMint` writes a mint record at an arbitrary 32-byte address, letting a caller clobber a deployed program's record or replace an existing mint's authority and supply, and `CreateAssociatedTokenAccount` resets an existing balance to zero. The equivalent out-of-process worker enforces the mint-authority and source-owner checks, so the control exists in the project but not on this path. Validation is by source trace: the crate does not build at this revision.

```suggestion
                    SvmInstructionEnvelope::SplMintTo {
                        mint,
                        dest_owner,
                        amount,
                    } => {
                        let mint_acct = read_svm_account(host, &mint).unwrap_or_default();
                        let recorded_authority = serde_json::from_slice::<serde_json::Value>(
                            &mint_acct.data,
                        )
                        .ok()
                        .and_then(|v| {
                            v.get("authority")
                                .and_then(|a| a.as_str())
                                .map(str::to_owned)
                        });
                        let expected = hex::encode(caller_pk);
                        if recorded_authority.as_deref() != Some(expected.as_str()) {
                            return Ok(EeOutcome {
                                status: OutcomeStatus::Revert,
                                output: b"mint authority mismatch".to_vec(),
                                gas_used: 9_000,
                            });
                        }
                        let Ok(ata) = derive_associated_token_address(&dest_owner, &mint) else {
                            return Ok(EeOutcome {
                                status: OutcomeStatus::Revert,
                                output: Vec::new(),
                                gas_used: 5_000,
                            });
                        };
                        let mut acc = read_svm_account(host, &ata).unwrap_or_default();
                        let cur = acc
                            .data
                            .get(..8)
                            .and_then(|s| <[u8; 8]>::try_from(s).ok())
                            .map_or(0u64, u64::from_le_bytes);
                        acc.owner = SVM_SPL_TOKEN_PROGRAM_ID;
                        acc.data = cur.saturating_add(amount).to_le_bytes().to_vec();
                        let _ = write_svm_account(host, &ata, &acc);
                        Ok(EeOutcome {
                            status: OutcomeStatus::Success,
                            output: ata.to_vec(),
                            gas_used: 9_000,
                        })
```

